```catala
declaration structure Stay:
  data arrival content date
  data departure content date

declaration scope Bad:
  output s content Stay

scope Bad:
  definition s equals #[json = "{\"arrival\": \"2020-01-01\"}"] Stay
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Bad --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to validate JSON:
│    Missing object field departure
│  
│  Expected JSON object of the form:
│    { "arrival": $date,
│      "departure": $date }
│    $date:
│      /* Catala date */
│      string
│      /* Accepts strings with the following format: YYYY-MM-DD, e.g.,
│         "1970-01-31" */
│      | { /* Accepts date objects: {"year":<int>, "month":<int>,
│             "day":<int>} */
│          "year": integer ∈ [0, 9999.000000],
│          "month": integer ∈ [1, 12],
│          "day": integer ∈ [1, 31] }
│
├─➤ tests/json/bad/literal.catala_en:10.65-69:
│    │
│ 10 │   definition s equals #[json = "{/"arrival/": /"2020-01-01/"}"] Stay
